      "id": "indiana-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://iga.in.gov/ic/2026/Title_1.html",
      "title": "The legal holidays of Indiana (IC 1-1-9-1(a), \"for all purposes\") that\n`us-federal-holidays` does not already close: Abraham Lincoln's Birthday\n(February 12, the Friday before when it falls on a Saturday and the Monday\nafter when on a Sunday, IC 1-1-9-1(b)), Good Friday and Election Day, \"the\nday of any general, municipal, or primary election\". Only the even-year\nprimary (the Tuesday after the first Monday in May) and general election\n(the Tuesday after the first Monday in November) are listed, from the\nelection calendar of IC 3-10, which is not vendored. Each `once` day is\nlisted from the date the vendored Code file was served (June 30, 2026) to\nthe end of 2050. Not modeled: municipal and special elections, and a day to\nwhich the governor shifts an observance (IC 1-1-9-2), which no vendored\nsource lists (a last day on one is the earlier date)."
    }
